(footprint "Ebyte_E72-2G4M20S1E"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "meshsat")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Ebyte E72-2G4M20S1E 2.4 GHz SoC module (TI CC2652P1FRGZ, 20 dBm, Zigbee 3.0 / Thread / BLE 5), 17.5 x 28.7 x 2.5 mm, 34 stamp-hole pads at 1.27 mm, PCB on-board antenna on the 11.7 mm end below pins 1 and 34. Dimensions from the E72-2G4M20S1E User Manual rev 1.1 (2021-02-20) section 3, size and pin definition: side pins start 3.04 from the antenna-far edge, top-row pins 3.04 from the side edges, module bottom pad 1.0 wide x 0.8 long with a 0.65 half-hole (top pad 0.8 x 0.5); the manual gives no carrier land pattern, so the lands here are 0.9 x 1.8, 0.8 inside and 1.0 outside the module edge. Pins: 1 GND, 2 DIO_7, 3 DIO_8, 4 DIO_9, 5 DIO_10, 6 DIO_11, 7 DIO_12, 8 DIO_13, 9 DIO_14, 10 DIO_15, 11 GND, 12 GND, 13 JTAG_TMSC, 14 JTAG_TCKC, 15 DIO_16 (JTAG_TDO), 16 DIO_17 (JTAG_TDI), 17 DIO_18, 18 DIO_19, 19 GND, 20 VCC (1.9 to 3.8 V, 3.3 V for full power), 21 DIO_20, 22 DIO_21, 23 GND, 24 RESET_N (active low), 25 DIO_22, 26 DIO_23, 27 DIO_24, 28 DIO_25, 29 DIO_26, 30 DIO_27, 31 DIO_28, 32 DIO_29, 33 DIO_30, 34 GND. Pin 1 at the right column bottom (antenna end), 1 to 12 up the right side, 13 to 22 along the far edge right to left, 23 to 34 down the left side. UART: any brought-out DIO by firmware (DIO_0 to DIO_6 are not on the pads); the module's internal RF switch is driven by DIO_6 and DIO_5 (TX: DIO_6 low, DIO_5 high; RX: DIO_6 high, DIO_5 low, manual section 5.2), no PA or LNA control pad exists and there is no IPEX. Rule area on all copper layers under the antenna end and 3 mm beyond it (the manual asks for no routing under the module and an exposed antenna, no figure given). Source: https://www.cdebyte.com/pdf-down.aspx?id=770 (vendor/zigbee/ebyte-e72-2g4m20s1e-user-manual.pdf)")
	(tags "Ebyte E72-2G4M20S1E CC2652P zigbee module stamp hole")
